My best friend @PERSON2 and I have a fun and unique tradition that we made up together. Every time she comes over to my house, we always slide down the stairs in a sleeping bag. It all started a few years ago, during the @TIME1 holiday season when she was spending the @TIME1 at my house. While we were sitting on the staircase with nothing to do, it suddenly hit me that we should turn the long staircase into our own personal playground. I turned to @PERSON2 and said, "@CAPS1, what could two little girls possibly do to have fun in the middle of the day? @CAPS4 All we have to work with is this long staircase that has been sitting right under our noses the whole time!" To which she replied, "I'm listening." We were both getting excited because we finally found something fun to do.

"I'll show you. We just need to get all the pillows we can find," I said. The two of us scampered around the house looking in every room and grabbed all the pillows we could find to set at the foot of the stairs. "What do we need all these pillows for?" @PERSON2 asked, surprised. "For padding," I said. Once the pillows were set up, I told her of my brilliant plan, and she loved it! We couldn't wait to get started. "@CAPS5 purple sleeping bag will be perfect for @TIME1," said @PERSON2. I ran down the hallway to my room and snatched my sleeping bag, and sprinted back towards the staircase. My purple sleeping bag is super slick and was just the thing we needed to glide down the stairs.

@DATE1 is the present day, and even though we are fourteen and fifteen @DATE1 old, we still have fun doing this. Over the @DATE1, we have improved it, making it nerve-racking and loads more fun. @PERSON2 and I have agreed on some safety precautions, which we thought were necessary. Initially, we just used the sleeping bag, and we didn't need any extra gear or padding. However, as we added on to it, we agreed to wear a helmet and sometimes add a few pillows. The helmet kind of scares my mom because it's never needed. 

One day, while my parents were out, @PERSON2 and I had been eating way too much sugar and were extremely hyper. The two of us were sliding down the stairs, but we wanted to make it even bigger and better than ever before! We started brainstorming. My brother's room was upstairs, and we somehow wanted to incorporate his mattress into our fun. So, @PERSON2 and I dragged the mattress out onto the staircase. We both sat down on the mattress, pushed off, and went shooting down the stairs. We could barely keep a hold of the mattress. The farther we went down the staircase, the farther we slid off of the mattress. We were laughing so hard that we almost slammed into the wall when we reached the bottom! It was so much fun. After that first ride, we decided we had better put an extra pillow up on the wall somehow. One thing we hadn't thought about before we went crashing down the stairs with the mattress was how heavy it was. It was very hard to get back up the stairs, but we didn't mind because we were having so much fun. 

@PERSON2 and I were getting tired, so we decided to take a break. The two of us hauled the mattress back upstairs and used it one last time before plopping down on the couch in the opposite room. Not too long ago, my mom had bought an inflatable exercise bean shaped just like a real bean and had handles on both sides. @PERSON2 started messing around with it, and she said, "Why don't you try it?" We both rushed back to the stairs, ready to have some more of the reckless fun that we love. Our imaginations were bouncing off the walls. This time, we felt it was time to mix everything together for the ultimate ride. We kept the mattress on the top of the stairs and measured out just where we needed my sleeping bag to be. Our idea was to be sitting on the exercise bean, on top of the mattress, slide down off the mattress, land on the sleeping bag waiting on the stairs to give us a turbo boost, and finally be sent flying into the pillows at the bottom of the staircase. I found some duct tape so that @PERSON2 could tape the sleeping bag to the floor. 

@PERSON2 let me go first. I was nervous because we'd never done anything like this before. After a minute, I finally pushed off. It was a bigger drop from the mattress to the stairs than I thought it would be. But when I landed on the sleeping bag, it was like being inside of a @PERSON1 video game and hitting the turbo boost. It was scary, but when I got to the bottom of the stairs, the two of us were laughing uncontrollably. We had so much fun.

They say laughter is the best medicine. @CAPS15 Personally, I think that's true. For one, jokes are a great thing for laughter, but it depends on the joke sometimes because some jokes are extremely funny while others are just plain horrible. Another reason why laughter is so great is that when you're laughing, that automatically means that you're in a good mood. @CAPS15 I love to be happy or in a good mood. I hate being all mad or upset. It's not me. I love it when I can't breathe because I am laughing so hard. Those are the best jokes, and you might even about wet yourself, especially if you're extremely ticklish. @CAPS15 I know quite a few people that are, and I feel sorry for them because I would be downright embarrassed if I wet myself in front of anyone. My whole life has had laughter in it. To me, anytime is laughter time.

Well, I have quite a few stories about laughter, but I am only gonna tell you one. @CAPS15 It's one of my favorites, when me and my friends are all hanging out at my grandmother's house for my 15th birthday party. @CAPS15 We're all having a great time on the homemade slip and slide, the food, and the drinks (soda, of course, not alcohol). But anyway, my cousin @PERSON1 has these games that he came up with, like the @CAPS1 relay, @CAPS2 fishing, @CAPS3 the gum in the whipped cream, and my favorite, @CAPS4.

@CAPS4 is a game where you can have as many players as you want. All the supplies you need are a lot of string, a lot of balloons, and one person to start out as the @CAPS4. Say you have two humans and one @CAPS4. All the humans would have balloons tied around their waists, and they all try to run away from the @CAPS4 and hide anywhere inside the boundaries. It doesn't matter how your balloon pops, who pops it, or what pops it; once it is popped, you are a @CAPS4 until there are only two humans left, and you start a new game. Now you might ask yourself why this is funny. Now I am gonna tell you why.

@CAPS15 We're all at my party having a great time, right? My cousin @PERSON1 says, "Who wants to play the game @CAPS4?" We all say, "Well, what's that?" He goes over all the rules like I said before, and we say, "Let's play." Me and my friend @CAPS9 are running away, and all of a sudden, we start hearing my cousin's @CAPS4 noise. That means he is coming, and he freaked out and ran away. When he leaves, you hear the screeching scream come out, and you hear his balloon pop; that means that he got out. We're all laughing because when he flew, he launched about three feet backward. It was the funniest thing ever because when I got over there, he was still on the ground, and everyone was trying to breathe. I swear I think everyone was about to wet themselves; they would've laughed some more if it wasn't for the game.

@CAPS15 My friend and I got up and started chasing people with my cousin @PERSON1 and the rest of us ran out of there as quickly as possible. Yet again, you hear my cousin making his @CAPS4 noise, people running and screaming, and my friend trying to make the same @CAPS4 noise but can't. One by one, I hear the balloons popping, and soon I was the last one left. I was gonna give up, but I am getting chased until I am completely out of breath. One of my friends @ORGANIZATION1 comes up in front of me, and I said, "I don't care, get me out. I wanna lay down." He took the balloon, popped it, and I asked, "Can I take a nap?" He said, "No, because we have to get ready for the next round. You better rest up quick or you'll be dogging." I rested up as much as I could before we got everyone strapped up for the next game.

I was hoping to get some kind of reward for winning the very first game of @CAPS4, but my cousin @PERSON1 had to be a smart alec about it, saying, "Getting to play the game isn't a big enough reward for you, stingy!" As always, everyone starts busting up laughing at every single little thing that my cousin @PERSON1 does, but I do have to admit that he is one of the funniest guys that I have ever met.

@CAPS15 There you go. There is my story about laughter, but I do have plenty more, but I think I've wasted too much of your time. That's all I have to say.

I believe that laughter and having a sense of humor is something that everyone generally has in common. Among young teenage girls, laughter is an infectious commodity that is always wonderful. It's the purest form of joy we have, bringing humans together and being the beginning and end of friendship and unity. Laughter can lift the spirits of those in need and make the worst day a little brighter. The kindness, generosity, and goodness of laughter are a few things that are right in the world today. Even in poverty, depression, and oppression, the simple joy of laughter can wash away a person's worries for a split second and fill us with utter warmth. 

@PERSON1 and I have been the best of friends since we were ten years old, and laughter has always been our strongest element. We have a knack for making each other burst out in laughter when all we want to do is be angry or cry. We've decided that apart, we're just a little funny, but with our powers combined, we could make anyone laugh. We use that power on each other when we're having bad days, or we simply need some cheering up. Laughter is what binds us together as best friends. We'd be different people if it wasn't for laughter. Even if I drifted from her, we'd always be cracking jokes, making each other's guts ache, and tearing up from laughing so hard. 

My first impression of @PERSON1 was of her stomping down to our neighborhood park to yell at her sister, whom I had been playing with. It would be self-explanatory why I didn't like her at first. Luckily, after going to @PERSON1's house with her sister, @PERSON1 and I found that we had many things in common, and we were only four months apart. That childish kind of cajoling held our friendship together, for it was a bit rocky in the beginning. Always fighting and arguing about things that now, we look back on and laugh at our adolescent stupidity. One time, she proceeded to tell me that I couldn't hear her because I had a big bug in my ear. Now we remind each other of things like that and have a good time laughing about it. We were mere @NUM1-year-olds then. Now, almost @NUM2, we rarely fight, but we always laugh and make the best of what we've got with our poking fun. Laughter was definitely the band-aid in the beginning of our rickety friendship. 

@PERSON1 has a gift for making anything funny at any time. She says the wrong (but hilarious) things, but always at the right time. Laughter is now a necessity between us, and it's what keeps our friendship so strong. I think about what the human race would be like if laughter was not a factor in everyday life. Everyone knows that it wasn't a good day if you haven't laughed or even smiled. People would be dull and unhappy. Laughter heals people from sickness and gives us hope that everything will be okay after all. It's healthy for you. With a flip of a switch, laughing can bring within us an ecstatic and serendipitous feeling. People take it for granted and use it for wrong when it's meant to spread the word of happiness. We're lucky to have a gift of such natural joy. Can anyone even explain, in detail, the feeling laughter truly brings us? I think not. It's like describing the scent of something; you just can't do it. The words aren't there. I think of those poor and miserable people that have forgotten what it feels like to laugh, and it's very sad. I strive to laugh every single day and make at least one other person laugh. What is a life without a diamond in the rough like laughter? It's not a life at all, for laughter will always be your shelter on the pursuit of happiness.

We all know how to laugh, and we have all probably laughed at least once in our lives. But I never laughed as hard as I did the day my friend @CAPS1 and I were waiting for our friends @LOCATION1, @PERSON2, and @PERSON3 to come back from getting @PERSON3 from @LOCATION3 to come and hang out for a little while.

